@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix semapv: <https://w3id.org/semapv/vocab/> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix sioc: <http://rdfs.org/sioc/ns#> .
@prefix nmo: <http://www.semanticdesktop.org/ontologies/2007/03/22/nmo#> .
@prefix ical: <http://www.w3.org/2002/12/cal/icaltzd#> .
@prefix wd: <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/> .

# Term equivalences for the email domain — GMEOW authoring source.
# Compiled to mappings/gmeow-email.sssom.tsv by `gmeow compile-mappings`.

gmeow:mapsetEmail a gmeow:MappingSet ;
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-email.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:setId "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/mappings/email" ;
    gmeow:license "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" ;
    gmeow:setComment "Email alignments. EmailMessage is equivalent to schema:EmailMessage; the rest use skos:closeMatch (cross-type/loose) to schema.org, the Nepomuk Message Ontology (NMO), and SIOC. The reified MessageParticipant relator is canonical; flat from/to/cc/bcc and their schema.org/NMO counterparts are lossy projection shortcuts. Trust terms (RelayHop/AuthenticationResult/signatures) are canonical — no maintained external RDF vocabulary exists for them. MessageParticipantRole envelope/resent roles are also canonical — no external vocabulary covers them. threadSubject and subjectPrefix are canonical — no maintained external vocabulary exposes thread-level normalized subject or per-message prefix stripping. MessageKind and its individuals are canonical — no maintained external vocabulary covers DSN/ARF/MDN/auto-generated report kinds. priority, importance, precedence, autoSubmitted, readReceiptRequested, and dispositionNotificationTo are canonical — no maintained external vocabulary covers these behavioral header facets. MIME body-part metadata terms (MultipartBodyPart, InlinePart, MultipartType, ContentDisposition, ContentTransferEncoding, hasMultipartType, hasInlinePart, hasContentDisposition, hasContentTransferEncoding, partId, contentId, charset; the design) are canonical — no maintained external RDF vocabulary covers granular MIME structure, Content-ID, transfer encoding, or disposition values. Mailbox hierarchy terms (parentMailbox, childMailbox, mailboxSortOrder, mailboxPath, mailboxTotalMessages, mailboxUnreadMessages; the design) are canonical — JMAP (RFC 8621) has no maintained RDF vocabulary. parentMailbox/childMailbox specialize the universal partOf/hasPart spine; path and counts are derived projection state (Principle 12). Calendar invitation bridge terms (describesEvent, calendarAttachment, calendarUid, CalendarMethod, hasCalendarMethod, messageKindCalendarInvitation; mail-corpus invitation consumer) are canonical — no maintained external RDF vocabulary covers the email→event bridge. iCalendar METHOD/UID alignments are by reference to icaltzd. Email versioning terms (EmailPatchDiff, hasPatchDiff, messageIdGenerated, messageIdCollision, canonicalFingerprint, bodyLineFingerprint, analysisScope, analysisInputBodyLine; the design) are canonical — no maintained external vocabulary covers Message-ID collision tracking, body-line fingerprinting, or email patch-diff artifacts. Canonical/variant status is represented via the cross-cutting VersionMembership relator from versions.ttl, not as email-specific subclasses. JMAP structural identifier terms (blobId, bodyStructure, BodyValue; the design) are canonical — JMAP (RFC 8620/8621) defines blobId, partId, and BodyStructure at the protocol level, but has no maintained RDF vocabulary. bodyStructure is a serialized projection; the canonical MIME tree is the existing hasBodyPart/hasPart spine (Principle 4).".

gmeow:EmailMessage owl:equivalentClass schema:EmailMessage {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-email.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 1.0
|} .

gmeow:EmailMessage skos:closeMatch nmo:Email {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-email.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.95
|} .

gmeow:EmailMessage skos:closeMatch sioc:Post {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-email.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.7
|} .

gmeow:Message skos:closeMatch schema:Message {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-email.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.9
|} .

gmeow:Message skos:closeMatch nmo:Message {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-email.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.9
|} .

gmeow:Thread skos:closeMatch sioc:Thread {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-email.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.8
|} .

gmeow:Mailbox skos:closeMatch nmo:Mailbox {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-email.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.85
|} .

